---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

/*
 * TODO (operator): before going live, add:
 *  - full name / company of the operator
 *  - postal address
 *  - authorised representatives and register entry, if applicable
 *  - name of the hosting provider (section "Hosting & server log files")
 * These details are required under Art. 13 GDPR.
 */

const toc = [
  { id: 'controller', label: 'Controller' },
  { id: 'principles', label: 'Overview & principles' },
  { id: 'hosting', label: 'Hosting & server logs' },
  { id: 'fonts', label: 'Google Fonts' },
  { id: 'local-storage', label: 'Browser storage' },
  { id: 'no-cookies', label: 'No cookies, no tracking' },
  { id: 'recipients', label: 'Recipients & disclosure' },
  { id: 'rights', label: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'security', label: 'Data security' },
  { id: 'children', label: 'Children' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What data is processed when you visit prozentrechner-online.com – and what is explicitly not. No cookies, no tracking, no user accounts."
  canonicalUrl="https://prozentrechner-online.com/en/privacy-policy"
  alternateUrls={{
    de: 'https://prozentrechner-online.com/datenschutz',
    en: 'https://prozentrechner-online.com/en/privacy-policy',
  }}
  breadcrumb="Privacy"
  toc={toc}
>
  <p>
    Protecting your personal data matters to us. This privacy policy explains transparently what
    data is processed when you visit this website – and what data is <strong>not</strong>
    processed. It applies to the entire {site.name} website.
  </p>

  <h2 id="controller">1. Controller</h2>
  <p>
    The controller responsible for data processing on this website within the meaning of the
    General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>{site.name}</strong><br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
  </p>

  <h2 id="principles">2. Overview &amp; principles</h2>
  <p>
    This website is a pure online calculation tool. There is <strong>no registration</strong>,
    <strong>no user accounts</strong>, <strong>no advertising</strong> and
    <strong>no analytics or marketing services</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    All calculations run entirely in your browser. The numbers you enter are
    <strong>not transmitted to our servers</strong>, not stored there and not evaluated. You can
    therefore use every calculator offline or with network traffic disabled once the page has
    loaded.
  </p>
  <div class="legal-note">
    In short: we do not profile you, we do not sell data, and we do not use tracking cookies.
    Only the technically necessary data that any website request produces is processed.
  </div>

  <h2 id="hosting">3. Hosting &amp; server log files</h2>
  <p>
    This website is hosted by an external hosting provider. When you access the website, the
    hosting provider automatically collects information transmitted by your browser and stores it
    in server log files. This includes in particular:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>IP address of the requesting device</li>
    <li>date and time of access</li>
    <li>name and URL of the file or page accessed</li>
    <li>amount of data transferred and the access status (e.g. HTTP status code)</li>
    <li>browser type and version as well as operating system</li>
    <li>referrer URL (the previously visited page)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Purpose:</strong> providing, securing and stabilising the website, and defending
    against and investigating attacks.<br />
    <strong>Legal basis:</strong> Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in secure and functional
    provision).<br />
    <strong>Retention:</strong> log files are deleted automatically after a short period. The exact
    duration depends on the settings and deletion routine of our hosting provider.
  </p>

  <h2 id="fonts">4. Google Fonts</h2>
  <p>
    To display fonts consistently, this website uses web fonts (“Google Fonts”) that are loaded
    from Google servers when the page is opened. Your IP address, among other data, is
    transmitted to Google in the process.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Provider:</strong> Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland.<br />
    <strong>Purpose:</strong> consistent and appealing typography.<br />
    <strong>Legal basis:</strong> Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in consistent
    presentation).<br />
    <strong>Note:</strong> the percentage calculations work entirely in your browser regardless.
    If you want to avoid the transfer to Google, you can block external fonts in your browser;
    the website remains usable.
  </p>

  <h2 id="local-storage">5. Browser storage (localStorage)</h2>
  <p>
    This website stores some information locally on your device in your browser’s
    <code>localStorage</code>. This data stays exclusively on your device and is
    <strong>not transmitted to us or to third parties</strong>. The following is stored:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Key</th>
        <th>Content</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>pct_theme</code></td>
        <td>Your selected colour theme</td>
        <td>Remembering your theme choice on your next visit</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>pct_calc_history_v1</code></td>
        <td>Your most recent calculations</td>
        <td>History for quick reference and reuse</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    <strong>Legal basis:</strong> § 25(2)(2) TDDDG (German Telecommunications Digital Services
    Data Protection Act) and Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. Storage is strictly necessary for the function you
    explicitly requested (theme selection, history feature) and therefore permitted without
    consent.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Deletion:</strong> you can clear the history at any time using the “Clear all” button
    in the history panel. All locally stored data also disappears when you clear the site data or
    cache in your browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2 id="no-cookies">6. No cookies, no tracking</h2>
  <p>
    This website uses <strong>no cookies</strong> at all – neither for analytics nor for
    marketing or advertising. We also do not use:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>web analytics services (e.g. Google Analytics or Matomo)</li>
    <li>advertising or retargeting networks</li>
    <li>social media plugins or tracking pixels</li>
    <li>fingerprinting or any other form of user profiling</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Because no consent-based cookies or comparable technologies are used, no cookie banner is
    required either.
  </p>

  <h2 id="recipients">7. Recipients &amp; disclosure of data</h2>
  <p>
    Your data is not disclosed to third parties except to the service providers that are
    technically necessary:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>our <strong>hosting provider</strong> (operation and provision of the website),</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> as part of the font loading described in section 4.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Where service providers act on our behalf, this is based on data processing agreements
    pursuant to Art. 28 GDPR. Your data is <strong>not sold</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the following rights regarding your personal data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> to the data processed (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
    <li><strong>Rectification</strong> of inaccurate or incomplete data (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
    <li><strong>Erasure</strong> of your data (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
    <li><strong>Restriction</strong> of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
    <li><strong>Data portability</strong> (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
    <li><strong>Objection</strong> to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
    <li><strong>Withdrawal</strong> of any consent given, with effect for the future (Art. 7(3) GDPR)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise your rights, an email to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> is
    sufficient. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory
    authority (Art. 77 GDPR) – the authority of your habitual residence or of our place of
    establishment.
  </p>
  <div class="legal-note">
    Since we do not collect personal data beyond the technically unavoidable server log files,
    access or erasure requests in practice usually relate to those logs and to the data stored
    purely locally in your own browser, which you can delete yourself at any time.
  </div>

  <h2 id="security">9. Data security</h2>
  <p>
    This website is served exclusively over an encrypted HTTPS connection (TLS/SSL), so data
    transmitted cannot normally be read by third parties. We also apply appropriate technical and
    organisational measures to protect the website against loss, manipulation and unauthorised
    access.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">10. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our website is not specifically directed at children and we do not knowingly collect personal
    data from children. Because no registration is possible and no personal data is actively
    requested, use by minors is unproblematic.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">11. Changes to this privacy policy</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this privacy policy when the legal situation, our services or the technology
    used change. The current version published on this page applies in each case.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
